{number: 161}
{title: Heaven Came Down}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O what a [C] wonderful, wonderful day,
Day I will never for-[G7] get;
After I'd wandered in darkness away,
Jesus my Savior I [C] met.
O what a tender, compassionate friend!
He met the [C7] need of my [F] heart;
Shadows dis-[C] pelling, with joy I am telling,
He [G7] made all the darkness de-[C] part!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Heaven came down and glory filled my soul,
When at the [G7] cross the Savior made me whole;
My sins were [C] washed away and my [F] night was turned to day,
[C] Heaven came down and [G7] glory filled my [C] soul!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Born [C] of the Spirit with life from above
Into God's fam'ly di-[G7] vine,
Justified fully thro' Calvary's love,
O what a standing is [C] mine!
And the trans-[C7] action so quickly was [F] made
When as a [C] sinner I came,
Took of the [G7] offer of grace He did proffer,
He [G7] saved me, O praise His dear [C] name!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Now [C] I've a hope that will surely endure
After the passing of [G7] time;
I have a future in heaven for sure,
There in those mansions sub-[C] lime.
And it's be-[C7] cause of that wonderful [F] day
When at the [C] cross I believed;
Riches e-[G7] ternal and blessings supernal
From [G7] His precious hand I re-[C] ceived.
{end_of_verse}
